Sadly , Pip has no fortune in any possible way .
Besides this , Pip seems to be a shy and intelligent kid .
He looks like a good boy that lives in hell and the Devil is his sister .
Nevertheless , the narrator is the true protagonist and the way he tells the actions is the reason why the story can connect with the reader .
And the author does not try to describe the protagonist with words , but with actions .
Also , the narrator mainly uses direct speech , but he only uses indirect speech on just a few occasions referring to his own words .
This exception can be read at the end of the first chapter , where the narrator answers the thief , writing that he said that he would get him the file , and that he would get him what broken bits of food he could , and he would come to the thief at the Battery .
Apart from this , he just writes exactly what the characters say .
Also , he describes his parents in a hilarious way , imaging his father as a square , stout , dark man , with curly black hair just looking at their tombstone .
These twisted and creative thoughts are spread all over the text , accompanied by even more twisted reflections , like at the end of the first chapters , when he describes the man who stole him as a man afraid of the dead bodies in the graveyard just because he saw him hugging himself .
The narrator does not make an effort to describe the other characters psychologically , he focuses on their appearance .
The narrator describes her as a woman that has earned a good reputation for being aggressive with his little brother .
And we know that Joe is a good man because the protagonist describes him as mild , good - natured , sweet - tempered , easy - going and foolish , but that is all we know about them .
Also , the way the characters talk is opposed to the way the narrator writes .
In fact , the dialogues of each character are not longer than more than two sentences , with the only exception of the thief , who talks about his partner in twelve long sentences with complex structures .
Having at that time to find out for myself what the expression meant , and knowing her to have a hard and heavy hand , and to be much in the habit of laying it on her husband as well as on me , I supposed that Joe Gargery and I were both brought up by hand . "
On the other hand , the dialogues are simple and shorter :
" Now lookee here , " he said , " the question being whether you 're to be let to live . You know
What is a file ? "
" Yes , sir . "
" And you know what wittles is ? "
" Yes , sir . "
Pip uses a rich vocabulary , using a lot of mental verbs and abstract concepts that are usually inspired by concrete things .
The marsh pointed out in the first chapter is a good example .
The thief said " Who d'ye with ? "
This is written as it is said , making it more realistic .
The events are narrated in a mysterious way , telling us what happened in a realistic story - line without flashbacks .
The story is narrated as it happened .
Also , the slow rhythm is adequate .
Too much mystery and just a few facts can be read in these chapters .
All I know is that this story will not have a happy ending .
Probably , the thief will take Pip on an unwanted adventure that will make him grow up faster .
Like another brick in the wall , another tombstone in the graveyard .
